from pathlib import Path
import html,json
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
load=lambda n:json.loads((R/n).read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
d=load('RESULTS.json');summary=load('SUMMARY.json');qual=load('COMPUTATION-QUALIFICATION.json');e=lambda x:html.escape(str(x));pct=lambda x:f'{100*x:.2f}%'
def table(h,rs):return '<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+e(v)+'</th>' for v in h)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+str(v)+'</td>' for v in row)+'</tr>' for row in rs)+'</tbody></table></div>'
def find(l,weight,threshold):return next(c for c in d['correction_cases'] if c['original_panel_index']==l['original_panel_index'] and c['view']==l['view'] and c['coverage']=='1' and c['direction']=='forward' and c['weight_ratio']==weight and c['threshold']==threshold)
body='<p class="muted">VOYNICH · FROZEN POWER-COST DIAGNOSTIC · v99</p><h1>Where does the sensitivity go?</h1><p class="notice"><strong>Diagnostic only. The v98 qualification remains FAIL.</strong> No acceptance gate, family or effect was relaxed, no robustness bank resumed, and no manuscript score was tested or rescored. Easier thresholds below answer counterfactual questions; they are not replacement acceptance screens.</p>'
body+='<p>Bath hand2/B/P and Starred hand3/B/P, H/F and middle definitions separate. Same first v98 pilot/calibration bank, same strict transition fibers and every v97 fixed effect/coverage case. Complete opening-family columns and original failures retained.</p>'
body+='<h2>Clean comparison: hold the alternative fixed, vary only correction</h2><p>All four columns use exactly the same pilot transform, calibration layouts and alternative probability law. Only the number of contrasts/error budget changes. Both signs remain in each diagnostic.</p>'
for weight in ['3/2','2']:
 body+='<h3>Full-coverage forward weight '+('1.5' if weight=='3/2' else '2')+'</h3>'+table(['Section','Reading','View','Target only','Target ×28','Opening search only','Opening search ×28'],[[e(l['section']),l['reading'],e(l['view']),*[pct(find(l,weight,t)['correct_direction_power']) for t in ['target_only','target_x28','search_only','search_x28']]] for l in d['layouts']])
body+='<p>At weight1.5, target-only power is86–95% even with transition constraints intact, versus3–16% under the full correction. This locates a large loss in multiplicity for the frozen alternatives. It does not make the discovered target a pre-specified independent question or justify removing the correction now.</p>'
body+='<h2>Two correction costs interact</h2><p>For this display, the staged sequence is target → panel-wide opening search → full28panel/view budget. A second sequence applies the panel budget first. Both sum to the same total loss, but their allocations differ; there is no unique additive causal percentage.</p>'
rows=[]
for l in d['layouts']:
 a=find(l,'3/2','target_only')['correct_direction_power'];b=find(l,'3/2','search_only')['correct_direction_power'];c=find(l,'3/2','target_x28')['correct_direction_power'];z=find(l,'3/2','search_x28')['correct_direction_power'];rows.append([e(l['section']),l['reading'],e(l['view']),f'{100*(a-z):.2f} pp',f'{100*(a-b):.2f} + {100*(b-z):.2f} pp',f'{100*(a-c):.2f} + {100*(c-z):.2f} pp'])
body+=table(['Section','Reading','View','Total diagnostic power loss','Search first + budget second','Budget first + search second'],rows)
body+='<details><summary>Thresholds and exact null rejection sizes</summary>'+table(['Panel','Reading','View','Threshold','Forward critical D','Reverse critical D','Strict-null rejection probability'],[[l['original_panel_index'],l['reading'],e(l['view']),e(k),e(v['forward_min']),e(v['reverse_max']),pct(v['exact_strict_null_size'])] for l in d['layouts'] for k,v in l['thresholds'].items()])+'</details><p>Target-only diagnostics spend more error probability on this one question. Their greater power is not a free gain available for the original data-driven search claim.</p>'
body+='<h2>What the transition constraints remove</h2><p>The relaxed comparison drops adjacent S/Q/N transition counts only. It keeps the same readable spans, literal endpoints, word multisets and unknown seams. Its exact class-count DP was qualified against direct authored enumeration before these diagnostics.</p>'
body+=table(['Section','Reading','View','Strict / relaxed variable spans','Strict / relaxed null SD','Variance retained','Log2 order-space removed'],[[e(l['section']),l['reading'],e(l['view']),str(l['constraints']['strict_variable_spans'])+' / '+str(l['constraints']['loose_variable_spans']),f'{l["constraints"]["strict_SD"]:.3f} / {l["constraints"]["loose_SD"]:.3f}',pct(l['constraints']['retained_variance_fraction']),f'{l["constraints"]["removed_log2_class_orders"]:.1f} bits'] for l in d['layouts']])
body+='<p>The constraints remove roughly34–44%of null score variance, as well as many admissible orders. That is real restriction, but space shrinkage is not the same as a percentage of power lost: constraints remove noise and possible signal together. Considerable targeted detection remains.</p>'
body+='<h2>Why a looser control cannot be treated as free extra power</h2><p>Tilting each model’s own null produces DIFFERENT alternative distributions. The next table is a descriptive generator comparison at an exact targeted.05 diagnostic, not a causal decomposition.</p>'
rows=[]
for l in d['layouts']:
 cs=[c for c in d['constraint_model_cases'] if c['original_panel_index']==l['original_panel_index'] and c['view']==l['view']];strict=next(c for c in cs if c['comparison']=='strict_own_base' and c['direction']=='forward' and c['weight_ratio']=='3/2');loose=next(c for c in cs if c['comparison']=='loose_own_base' and c['direction']=='forward' and c['weight_ratio']=='3/2');cross=next(c for c in cs if c['comparison']=='strict_alternative_loose_test' and c['direction']=='null');same=next(c for c in cs if c['comparison']=='strict_alternative_loose_test' and c['direction']=='forward' and c['weight_ratio']=='3/2');rows.append([e(l['section']),l['reading'],e(l['view']),pct(strict['correct_direction_power']),pct(loose['correct_direction_power']),pct(cross['any_rejection']),pct(same['correct_direction_power'])])
body+=table(['Section','Reading','View','Strict own-tilt power1.5','Relaxed own-tilt power1.5','Strict r1 background rejected by relaxed test','Same strict tilted law tested against relaxed null'],rows)
body+='<p>The relaxed test can reject local-transition background even when no extra residual tilt was introduced: up to52%in the bath middle-N diagnostic. This is not miscalibration under its own null—the strict law is a different distribution. It is a warning against interpreting that rejection as evidence of higher-order residual structure. Removing constraints changes the question.</p><p>The exact targeted test here centres on its own null mean; the correction ladder above uses the unchanged v98 pilot. Do not mix these baselines into a single arithmetic attribution.</p>'
body+='<h2>Checks, failures and complete ledgers</h2>'+table(['Check','Result'],[['Loose DP authored sequences',qual['authored_sequences']],['Authored fibers',qual['fibers']],['Exact view checks',qual['view_checks']],['Full v98 power replay','All312original cases unchanged'],['Diagnostic correction cases',len(d['correction_cases'])],['Constraint/model-mismatch cases',len(d['constraint_model_cases'])],['Manuscript rescoring / revised gates','NONE']])
body+='<details><summary>All correction cases, including reverse/partial/null failures</summary>'+table(['Panel','View','Coverage','Direction','Weight','Threshold','Power','Null/any rejection'],[[c['original_panel_index'],e(c['view']),e(c['coverage']),c['direction'],e(c['weight_ratio']),e(c['threshold']),pct(c['correct_direction_power']),pct(c['any_rejection'])] for c in d['correction_cases']])+'</details>'
body+='<p>The clean comparison shows a large multiplicity cost; the structural comparison shows meaningful restriction but not elimination of information. It does not yield a unique causal fraction attributable to each. Both are conditional diagnostics on exposed layouts and one bank perpanel. No original source score, p-value or failed qualification status changes.</p><p><a href="PROTOCOL.json">Pre-calculation frozen diagnostic</a> · <a href="FREEZE.json">Source/bank/script hashes</a> · <a href="RESULTS.json">All cases and structural ledgers</a> · <a href="LOOSE-NULLS.json">Exact relaxed null weights</a> · <a href="VERIFICATION.json">Independent replay</a> · <a href="../transition-maxT-qual-v98/report.html">Unchanged failed v98 qualification</a></p><p>Browser appearance unreviewed; numerical and source verification are separate.</p>'
css='''<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark;--bg:light-dark(#f5f2e9,#18251f);--fg:light-dark(#203f35,#e2e9df);--sub:light-dark(#54695b,#b4c7b7);--rule:light-dark(#c0ccbd,#48604d);--fill:light-dark(#e5ebda,#2a3e2d)}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font:16px/1.55 system-ui}main{max-width:1450px;padding:30px;margin:auto}h1{font-size:32px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:23px;margin-top:30px}p{max-width:1100px}a{color:inherit}.muted{color:var(--sub)}.notice{padding:16px;background:var(--fill)}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:9px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}summary{cursor:pointer}details{margin:16px 0}@media(max-width:700px){main{padding:16px}}</style>'''
(R/'report.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Transition versus search power cost · v99</title>'+css+'</head><body><main>'+body+'</main></body></html>',encoding='utf-8');print('Frozen diagnostic report written; v98 gates and source scores untouched.')
